{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina","id":291855,"title":"New Orleans after Katrina?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-25T01:00:34-07:00","id":291855,"title":"New Orleans after Katrina?","content":"I was reading the Strix Chronicle Anthology and read one of the stories which had New Orleans after Katrina hit. It seemed to imply Baron Cimetiere was no longer around, but that Vidal was still in charge. I thought that was pretty cool.<br /> <br /> I know we don't do metaplot in nWoD and we don't like it, but if anyone around has some idea of the New Orleans draft sitting around, would you be willing to share what the writers personally envisioned for the fate of the city? I don't particularly want it as some sort of gospel, but having some ideas of how things might've gotten shaken up would be dope.<br /> <br /> I'd also love whatever thoughts you guys want to share for what to do with New Orleans circa 2014.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T01:38:37-07:00","id":291880,"title":"","content":"Here's a nice page of <a href=\"http://www.thegatewaypundit.com/2005/09/more-hurricane-katrina-folklore-vs-fact-2/?PageSpeed=noscript\" target=\"_blank\">Katrina fact vs fiction.</a> In my WoD, all the fiction is true. There really are roving cannibal gangs.<br /> <br /> I always thought that Katrina and shortly after post-Katrina might make a good &quot;zombie apocalypse&quot; story but the hurricane and humans instead of zombies. Fortify a place against raids and the weather, go out scavenging for supplies. To add supernatural spice, New Orelan's thriving occult community has been decimated; various experiments, imprisoned monsters and servants have gotten loose.<br /> <br /> I know this sounds more Hunter than Vampire, I'm not really a vampire sort of guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:00:31-07:00","id":292668,"title":"","content":"Pandora's Book for the Promethean line has a story outline in the Appendix where the setting is post-Katrina New Orleans. Specifically, it's set pretty shortly after Katrina. Unfortunately it's pretty sparse in terms of details on how the setting has changed from the original write-up in the VtR core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:32:50-07:00","id":292962,"title":"","content":"<i>Secrets of the Covenants</i> has some fiction taking place in modern New Orleans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T07:35:20-07:00","id":292963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=292962#post292962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Secrets of the Covenants</i> has some fiction taking place in modern New Orleans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it also feature Chicago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T13:13:00-07:00","id":293159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=292962#post292962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Secrets of the Covenants</i> has some fiction taking place in modern New Orleans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you teasing Dev - pics or it didn't happen! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:49:05-08:00","id":302234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=292963#post292963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it also feature Chicago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not extensively, but Solomon Birch is in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T09:16:46-08:00","id":302287,"title":"","content":"Random little tidbit for people who want to run games:<br /> <br /> Right after Katrina, there was a large influx of immigrants from out of state and country as part of the rebuilding effort (a lot of people had to be brought in to do the physical construction). The majority of these workers were Hispanic, leading to a sudden increase in Hispanic population and culture.<br /> <br /> Which means that, among other things, you can finally get good Mexican and South American food back home. This being the South, this has of course caused some racial tensions. I recall visiting home for Christmas a few years post-Katrina and overhearing the following conversation at a party:<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you see that they started putting advertisements in the paper in Spanish?&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish they wouldn't do that. I think it's going to attract the Wrong Sort of People.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ahhh. My hometown.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, we can do several things with this. We want to be careful and respectful (no WoD: Gypsies please), but think of themes that you can replicate. With any large influx of people, vampires are naturally going to follow. Carpetbaggers of every stripe can rush into the city, helping to rebuild but also wanting to bring a little bit of home with them. The Invictus of Baton Rouge might step in. Help from Circle of the Crone witches from Austin or Houston. Maybe a more Baptist sect of the et Sanctum rolls into town offering succor.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, this could be another supernatural race entirely who seek to clean up the mess that is naturally left by any major disaster. When I ran a post-Katrina game, I actually chose Sin-Eaters. Not only did it make sense culturally (Geist is super Day of the Dead-y), but it also made sense from a plot standpoint. After that flood, the city was going to be LOUSY with the ghosts of the drowned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T13:12:41-08:00","id":302569,"title":"","content":"Also Clanbook Mekhet has a side story about an elder waking up after Katrina. Written by Christopher Wilde. It's pretty awesome and a very sympathetic character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T19:13:11-08:00","id":302853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>underwoodfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=302287#post302287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random little tidbit for people who want to run games:<br /> <br /> Right after Katrina, there was a large influx of immigrants from out of state and country as part of the rebuilding effort (a lot of people had to be brought in to do the physical construction). The majority of these workers were Hispanic, leading to a sudden increase in Hispanic population and culture.<br /> <br /> Which means that, among other things, you can finally get good Mexican and South American food back home. This being the South, this has of course caused some racial tensions. I recall visiting home for Christmas a few years post-Katrina and overhearing the following conversation at a party:<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you see that they started putting advertisements in the paper in Spanish?&quot;<br /> &quot;I wish they wouldn't do that. I think it's going to attract the Wrong Sort of People.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ahhh. My hometown.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness, we can do several things with this. We want to be careful and respectful (no WoD: Gypsies please), but think of themes that you can replicate. With any large influx of people, vampires are naturally going to follow. Carpetbaggers of every stripe can rush into the city, helping to rebuild but also wanting to bring a little bit of home with them. The Invictus of Baton Rouge might step in. Help from Circle of the Crone witches from Austin or Houston. Maybe a more Baptist sect of the et Sanctum rolls into town offering succor.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, this could be another supernatural race entirely who seek to clean up the mess that is naturally left by any major disaster. When I ran a post-Katrina game, I actually chose Sin-Eaters. Not only did it make sense culturally (Geist is super Day of the Dead-y), but it also made sense from a plot standpoint. After that flood, the city was going to be LOUSY with the ghosts of the drowned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the Prince was on the verge of a psychotic break down before Katrina, I think the influx of new beliefs that may contradict his catholic ideals, accompanied by the decimation of most of his empire he spent centuries building would not have very pretty results for the Kindred population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T02:48:47-08:00","id":303147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [...]I think the influx of new beliefs that may contradict his catholic ideals,[...] </div> </div> </div>Aren't most hispanics catholic? And Vidal himself is spanish as is Maldonato.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T05:41:00-08:00","id":303212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=302853#post302853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Considering the Prince was on the verge of a psychotic break down before Katrina, I think the influx of new beliefs that may contradict his catholic ideals, accompanied by the decimation of most of his empire he spent centuries building would not have very pretty results for the Kindred population.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the idea that an influx of kine with believes that Vidal doesn't share wouldn't drive him crazy, and that it's vastly overstating the issue to suggest that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=303147#post303147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't most hispanics catholic? And Vidal himself is spanish as is Maldonato.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Catholicism is the dominant religion of Mexico, with around 80% of the population describing themselves as Catholics.<br /> <br /> It does bear mentioning that Vidal is a Spaniard, and that the relationship between Spaniards and the nations of Central and South America are not perfect, culturally. They're kine, so it's not likely that he really cares about them, but if you're looking for an attitude he might have, he could easily be dismissive and disdainful. Or he doesn't care beyond how they might benefit him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-05T06:15:04-08:00","id":303225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=303147#post303147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't most hispanics catholic? And Vidal himself is spanish as is Maldonato.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he speaks about the new influx of kindred following the mortal trail, not the mortals themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/824-araknee","name":"Araknee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T20:21:05-08:00","id":316885,"title":"","content":"Also, the portrayal of Vidal as a faithful Catholic doesn't at all jibe with the Sanctified Church as it currently stands. The two really aren't compatible in anyway, and the Sanctified are explicitly forbidden from engaging in mortal worship, as they are not privy to Christian salvation.<br /> <br /> I'm running a game in post-Katrina New Orleans right now, using much of the setting as presented in the book, but with the following changes:<br /> <br /> * Vidal is officially Prince-Archbishop, a rare combination of temporal and spiritual authority combined in one office, and the domain is set up like the Papal States or the clerical domains of the Holy Roman Empire. He's assisted by Bishop Maldonato and potentially one or more other subordinate bishops, as they function in a civil administrative capacity as much as they do in overseeing the individual Sanctified congregations. All NPCs with status among the Sanctified are technically priests. Lots of influence from the <i>Borgia</i> TV show there. Indeed, it's why Vidal is known by the epithet &quot;the Catholic&quot;: his views on the inseparability of church and state smack most modern American Kindred as a kind of Papism, whereas the First Estate would prefer that the Second know its place and leave temporal government in their capable hands.<br /> <br /> * I replaced John Marrow with Solomon Birch\u2014partly because I don't think it's kosher for a Sanctified priest to also be a Catholic priest, and partly because Birch is just more badass. He believes that he deserves a bishopric but has been denied one, so now he's supporting Savoy in an attempt to bypass the local Sanctified hierarchy altogether. He also makes a pretty frightening enforcer while also putting the lie to Savoy's claims to support religious tolerance. I had him bump off Gutterball Elgin, since I didn't have a use for that character, and it leaves the Master of Elysium title open. Perhaps Pierpont McGinn will go for it, as a way to cover his tracks as he moves between camps.<br /> <br /> * Savoy is still around, but he's making his move in the wake of Katrina and is either going to take the city or go down trying. If he does take it, the disparate and mutually antagonistic group of allies he's thrown together out of convenience will immediately go to war with itself, meaning that his reign will likely prove short.<br /> <br /> * I've alluded to Sister Snow as another up and coming force in the local Church, but I don't know anything about her beyond her vague mention in the blood sorcery book. I imagine she'll be a foil for Birch.<br /> <br /> * Baron Cimiti\u00e8re's faction effectively comprises its own minor covenant, which is independent from the mainline Circle of the Crone under Nathanial Branch, with an explicit racial division between the two (black and mixed-race voodoo practitioners on the one hand, with Branch's group being white and taking inspiration from a mixture of European witchcraft and Choctaw practices--basically the witches from the TV show <i>Salem</i>). The Baron claims the Trem\u00e9 as his domain, with Rampart St. forming a significant border between his world and that of the Quarter, since it's where the old wall used to be, which separated the town proper from Congo Square where the slaves danced and drummed. Branch's group practice in secret, since they have to live among the Sanctified.<br /> <br /> * The vast majority of the city's Kindred are at least nominal believers in the Sanctified religion, and most attend midnight mass. There are a few holdouts, but the local politics is set up so as to prevent them from advancing without toeing the line. Voodoo is generally driven underground outside of the Baron's territory, and outright paganism and witchcraft is actively suppressed in the most harsh terms, meaning that Blanch's coven is forced to keep an even lower profile. As Gangrel priscus, Blanch is a fixture in local politics even if he's not on the council, and he remains a thorn in Vidal's side. In general, Nosferatu and Gangrel are at the bottom of the New Orleans Kindred totem pole, since Vidal regards them as a bunch of unclean witches and heathens, whereas Ventrue and Daeva are the clans of prestige, with Mekhet occupying a middle ground with no collective reputation either way.<br /> <br /> * Striges started appearing in New Orleans prior to the hurricane, and groups of them have been seen to gather in the mostly-abandoned city in the nights since the levee broke, as if they anticipated the disaster. Or one to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 11-20-2014, 07:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T15:10:13-07:00","id":587453,"title":"","content":"I plan to run a New Orlean SAS adventure from <b>Beast</b> corebook, so I would like some points on running the setting after Kathrina.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Flag</b>, basically, your New Orlean post Kathrina is Papal State surounded by the pagan voodoo heretics?<br /> <br /> Who of big NPC from the <b>City of Damned:</b> <b>New Orlean </b>official setting would be dead in Kathrina?<br /> <br /> What would be views of Kindred powerplayers on beasts as whole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T17:17:26-07:00","id":587526,"title":"","content":"One of my players is planning on making a V:tR game taking place in New Orleans. We want to see what happened to Vidal and how is the city doing after Katrina. Does he continue to rule or went into torpor? If he went into torpor, who's the new prince? In this part we want to see who's running for prince, Savoy or one of Vidal's people. Also we want to see what is Sam, the Gangrel going to do? Is he going to let things continue or change things? <br /> <br /> I'm super curious and excited what my friend is going to do for our game. Also, by any chance is there going to be a new supplement setting for New Orleans? I really love City of the Damned: New Orleans; it's one my favorite supplements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T15:10:13-07:00","id":589593,"title":"","content":"Anyone uses some of the NPCs of the <i>Danse de la Mort</i> intro chronicle? Could be a bit of a spammer in the works to make a whole coterie of neonates at once in this context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-26-2015, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T14:23:33-07:00","id":593147,"title":"","content":"I have question on the numbers of vampires after Katrina. If we assume with those numbers before Hurricane has gone for a city...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/578305-how-many-monsters-are-in-your-city?p=590544#post590544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we go with 1/10 of &quot;touched by supernatural&quot; as proper Major Templetes we end with those numbers...<br /> (...)<br /> 600 proper monsters in New Orlean area. Going by previous spread it would be like 200 vampires, 40 werewolves, 28 mages, 8 prometheans, 80 changelings, 80 Sin-Eaters, 4 mummies, 20 demons and 100 beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>How many of those vampires would return to it? With all the damage and low mortals population to feed off.<br /> <br /> Also, taking in consideration Vidal &quot;Papal State&quot; of Lancea et Sactum domain serounded by Circle of Crone voodoo cults in it. How in this would Invictus, Ordo Dracul and Carthian Movement work in to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-16-2015, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T21:45:33-07:00","id":601396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/291855-new-orleans-after-katrina?p=593147#post593147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How many of those vampires would return to it? With all the damage and low mortals population to feed off.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game they had a rough patch in the couple of months after the storm, where it was almost post-apocalyptic. A number of vampires died. Others left. Those that remained were desperate for blood and took to poaching as the viable feeding grounds shrank to a sliver by the river. Vidal granted broad feeding rights in the Superdome (hence the horror stories about stuff that went on there). Over time things normalized, so by early 2006 things had reached a sustainable equilibrium, but only because a number of vamps had passed on (making room for the PCs in terms of territory and influence).<br /> <br /> The only named character I killed offscreen was Gus Elgin, whom Birch apparently burned as a Strix. The upshot was that the Sanctified lost a number of priests during the storm and its aftermath, undermining their hold on the city, particularly in the Uptown/Carrolton and lakeside neighborhoods. As a result Vidal was forced to grant certain areas to Invictus and Carthian interests, in order to make sure <i>someone </i>was in charge of major neighborhoods. Pierpont McGInn got much of Uptown, while my newbie PC Carthians (headed by a Ventrue) got the university/Audubon neighborhood, which they later expanded through judicious plotting.<br /> <br /> I don't have a hard number, but I assume there are around a hundred vamps currently in the city proper, possibly twice that in the metro area. I imagine that's as few as half, maybe two-thirds of the previous number. My assumption is that vampires have always been thicker on the ground in the Big Easy than just about anywhere else, since it's so much easier for them to blend in. The thing is, most of the dead vamps were Sanctified, which has led some to wonder if all of those were really just because of the flood. (They weren't.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, taking in consideration Vidal &quot;Papal State&quot; of Lancea et Sactum domain serounded by Circle of Crone voodoo cults in it. How in this would Invictus, Ordo Dracul and Carthian Movement work in to? </div> </div> </div>The Ordo Dracul is basically illegal. They operate out of a mansion in the Audubon neighborhood by Tulane at the sufferance of the aforementioned Carthian Ventrue PC, with whom they've made a mutually beneficial pact. The Ordo is mostly apolitical and dedicated to survival and research, but Kendall would like to pull them towards the Baron, whereas John Polk (a name I swiped from the 1st edition core) is looking to veer them towards allegiance with the Invictus.<br /> <br /> The Invictus in my game started from a position of ascendancy, having gained ground post-Katrina against the Sanctified rulers. However, my PCs worked pretty hard towards McGinn's undoing, at which point the Carthians gained ground and Pearl Chastain experienced a sort of renewal and took the reins of the Inner Circle. That wasn't to last in my game either, as she overplayed her hand in destroying Savoy and underestimated my Carthian PCs' resourcefulness and hatred of the First Estate. However, my game aside, I see Pearl as a major long-term player once McGinn is removed from the picture. She'll almost certainly outlast Savoy and make a play for the Quarter on the pretext of her relationship with its previous lord.<br /> <br /> The Carthians in my NO are rising fast, mostly due to PC activities. They've set up a kind of autonomous commune in Uptown and laid down laws that grant feeding rights to those who put in a certain amount of work for the cause. Much of that work has taken the form of trying to render the Invictus obselete, which means setting up things like clean-up crews, fake IDs, and all the other little quality of unlife services that the First Estate is used to monopolizing\u2014and offering it at a <i>much </i>lower price. That has led to some cold-war-style clashes, where at least one Invictus Young Turk tried to use the post-Katrina real estate market to torpedo the Carthian resource base. Like many of their enemies, he's not around anymore.<br /> <br /> For Vidal's part, he's been playing the Carthians and Invictus off each other while he can rebuild his own power base. Both are ostensibly loyal to him, but he knows the First Estate has ties to their allies in Baton Rouge and would love to see an overthrow of the Sanctified Papal States in NO. The Carthians have heretofore been mostly reformist rather than revolutionary, but that's not likely to last forever, and the storm and fierce competition for food has radicalized a number of young Kindred. Coco's still in his camp, but her influence is waning as the radicals look to other leaders. Vidal's best bet is to stall for time by letting the Carthians and Invictus go after each other. Meanwhile he tries not to let either side control too much of the city, and he only authorizes Sanctified Embraces.<br /> <br /> It didn't take long for Savoy to bite the dust in our game, thanks to a combination of plotting by Vidal and Chastain (who didn't realize Vidal's part until it was too late). Donovan is now lord of the French Quarter, having claimed it by right of inheritance and by killing his sire by his own hand once Savoy was officially branded a heretic for his dealings with the vouduisante Rosa Bale. My PCs arranged for Pearl to be undone immediately thereafter, so she didn't get to enjoy her victory and ended up a casualty of an even greater plot. Otherwise she quite possibly would have challenged Donovan's claim and won. That sent the Invictus into disarray, from which it still hasn't recovered.<br /> <br /> The only reason the Baron didn't come out on top of all this is that he was waging constant gang warfare with Savoy's camp for months after the storm <i>and </i>dealing with attacks from rival voodoo queen Rosa Bale, who still remains at large and still wants to unseat him. But for the most part New Orleans is once again a city with two power centers instead of three (i.e. Vidal and the Baron), and we all know how stable <i>that </i>setup is. As for Vidal, he <i>ought </i>to be taking his rest, but he's just growing more reclusive and taking ever harsher measures to keep his kingdom together. There's nothing to <i>force </i>him to go torpid, except that soon his dietary needs will be common knowledge, and the Kindred of the city whisper that something's not right with him. The PCs are wondering whether that thing that happened back in Storyville (which they found out about) didn't change him in deeper ways, or if maybe that's not even Vidal in there anymore...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":352,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","user":"Black Flag","date":". 07-24-2015, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T19:05:02-07:00","id":615901,"title":"","content":"Somebody told me New Orleans gets mentioned in Clanbook Ventrue. Did any of you read it? Does anybody know if there are further mentions in other supplements?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T19:52:41-07:00","id":615927,"title":"","content":"Several of the clanbooks have some reference to it. <i>Ventrue </i>has some correspondences regarding a covert action against New Orleans from another city (probably Houston) during the chaos caused by Katrina. <i>Gangrel</i> has a brief reminiscence by one who left the city after the storm to become nomadic again, having decided it was too full of bad memories. <i>Mekhet </i>has a first-person account of a long-torpid fellow who is awakened by the flood and shares some of his impressions of the city in the immediate aftermath. Seems Vidal and the Baron are still around but no mention of Savoy, who is presumably out of the picture by that point. <i>Nosferatu </i>deals with the retrieval from New Orleans of the Glass Harmonium, an artifact that also shows up in <i>Gangrel </i>and elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The New Orleans stuff is on the level of Easter eggs and some hints about how some of the bits might tie together, but it's more likely to tease your imagination than offer any specific details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T06:26:32-07:00","id":616380,"title":"","content":"A friend told me there is a Voodoo section in either Ancient Mysteries or Ancient Bloodlines. Could someone point me which one is it? Also, is Baron Cimitiere's faction mentioned in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T07:10:39-07:00","id":616421,"title":"","content":"One of the Promethean supplements, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/23079/Pandoras-Book?cPath=1_678&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">(Pandora's Book)</a>, also has a SAS set in/around New Orleans but it's...still early days as far as the 'clean up' goes. The sidebar on page 118 (120 for pdf) has some great ideas on how to adapt City of the Damned: New Orleans &amp; the V:tR Core (1st ed) books to the 'updated' setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}